Found by lane-unused while doing B099, 2026-08-31. Reported as a SEPARATE gap
rather than folded in, which was the right call -- B099 is a mislabelled
producer, this is a MISSING one, and they have nothing in common but the
completion entry point.

## What it is

`complete_namespace_members` resolves `Ns::` through
`TypeIndex::source_scope_members`, and that function is TYPEDB-ONLY. There is
no workspace route into it at all. So given a plugin that declares

    namespace Helper { void DoThing() {} }

typing `Helper::` offers **nothing**. Not a mislabelled entry, not a partial
list -- zero completions.

## Why the B099 ticket was wrong about this, and why that matters

B099's test plan asked for "a workspace namespace" as a third route into
`source_scope_members` alongside the typedb routes. That route does not exist.
The lane MEASURED that rather than working around it, and pinned the emptiness
with a PREMISE ASSERTION -- the test first proves the workspace really declares
the member, so the empty completion list cannot be a setup failure quietly
passing as a finding. That is the correct shape for a test whose subject is an
absence, and whoever fixes B107 should keep it: the moment a producer exists,
that test must be updated deliberately rather than silently starting to pass
for the wrong reason.

## Related, and worth reading before starting

- B099 (just landed): `source_scope_members` now returns
  `(String, ScopeMemberKind)`, so a new workspace producer must supply a kind
  rather than defaulting everything to FUNCTION -- the exact defect B099 fixed.
  Do not reintroduce it on the new path.
- B099 also surfaced a real collision to respect: `UI::Font` is BOTH a class
  and a namespace (`UI::Font::Default` hangs three accessors off it).
  Declaration wins, spelled as explicit `or_insert` precedence in fixed source
  order rather than relying on loop order. A workspace producer merging into
  the same map has to honour that precedence, and a workspace/typedb collision
  on the same name is the case to think about first.
- B013 closed "unknown namespaced symbols in user namespaces stay silent"
  (GH #58) on the CHECKING side. This is the same blind spot on the COMPLETION
  side, so B013's resolution machinery is the obvious place to look for an
  existing workspace-namespace member enumeration to reuse rather than write a
  second one. A rule living at one of N sites is the recurring defect shape in
  this repo (B073, B076, B098).
- B088: enum values reached `::` completion by a branch that runs BEFORE the
  scope walk, because an enum is not a scope. Confirmed by lane-unused as a
  genuinely separate path, not a second half of this one -- so do not try to
  unify them without measuring.

## Test shapes to generalise (per repo CLAUDE.md)

A one-level workspace namespace; a nested one (`A::B::`); a workspace namespace
whose name also exists in the typedb (collision, both directions); a namespace
containing a function, a class, an enum, an interface, a nested namespace, and
a global -- each asserted with its CORRECT kind, not merely present; a
namespace declared across two files; one behind the GH #58 closure fence; and a
negative control where nothing is declared, so a producer that returns
everything unconditionally does not score as a pass.